<article class="env-lemma" id="03X4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03X4">Lemma <span data-tag="03X4">35.31.2</span>.</a> The property $\mathcal{P}(f)=$“$f$ is locally quasi-finite” is étale local on the source. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We are going to use Lemma <a href="/tag/036H" data-tag="036H">35.26.4</a>. By Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01TK" data-tag="01TK">29.21.11</a> the property of being locally quasi-finite is local for Zariski on source and target. By Morphisms, Lemmas <a href="/tag/01TL" data-tag="01TL">29.21.12</a> and <a href="/tag/03WS" data-tag="03WS">29.37.6</a> we see the precomposition of a locally quasi-finite morphism by an étale morphism is locally quasi-finite. Finally, suppose that $X \to Y$ is a morphism of affine schemes and that $X' \to X$ is a surjective étale morphism of affine schemes such that $X' \to Y$ is locally quasi-finite. Then $X' \to Y$ is of finite type, and by Lemma <a href="/tag/0367" data-tag="0367">35.14.2</a> we see that $X \to Y$ is of finite type also. Moreover, by assumption $X' \to Y$ has finite fibres, and hence $X \to Y$ has finite fibres also. We conclude that $X \to Y$ is quasi-finite by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02NH" data-tag="02NH">29.21.10</a>. This proves the last assumption of Lemma <a href="/tag/036H" data-tag="036H">35.26.4</a> and finishes the proof. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>